A||N||10||Seanh||Oil comming out of oil cap?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||06-05-2001||11:45 AM||||I just noticed this on the 87 2.8 after taking it on about a 200 mile highway trip, there is quite a bit of oil comming out of the oil cap and leaking all over the valve covers. What is the problem? Please don't tell me this is sysptoms of blow-by! If it is indeed blow-by, shouldn't I actually notice increased oil pressure? The engine has 120 psi compression in all cylinders, and new head gaskets. Whats going on? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||06-05-2001||11:48 AM||||Change the PCV Filter and PCV Valve. If it still happens then your compression rings are worn out. ||||reg||3
Z||000002||Seanh||06-05-2001||11:57 AM||||Where is the PCV filter? Sorry, Iv never messed with that, or heard of it on this car for that matter. I did change the PCV valve, but it didn't seem to help much. Im gonna shoot this damn car already!||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||06-05-2001||12:01 PM||||How about getting a new oil cap ?<P>Could be that the gasket is shot...either has cracks in it or doesn't seal properly any more.<P>If your PCV and breather grommets are sealing okay, oil could just be finding the easiest way out, which could be the gasket on the oil cap.<P>You could probably just get another oil cap gasket too. A cheap option that might solve your problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||06-05-2001||12:15 PM||||You guys are right. Sorry didnt mean to get you uptight by jumping the gun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Check the cap, grommets and cover gaskets. IF there is oil barfing out the PCV filter and there are no leaks, then I would suspect rings.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000005||fierogt88||06-05-2001||02:22 PM||||I have this problem too!  is there an easy way to check the PCV valve/filter?||||reg||11
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||06-05-2001||02:27 PM||||if you take it off and it rattles its 99% proability of being ok.<P> but they only cost $3 or so, if you get your hands all greasy taking it off - might as well put a new one on.<P>  I have no idea what this PVC filter is thought, is it in the same hose going to the air intake plenium?||||reg||1
Z||000007||84Bill||06-05-2001||03:48 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>if you take it off and it rattles its 99% proability of being ok.<P> but they only cost $3 or so, if you get your hands all greasy taking it off - might as well put a new one on.<P>  I have no idea what this PVC filter is thought, is it in the same hose going to the air intake plenium?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>BUT if the spring is weak it will rattle and still be bad   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Better to just pay the 3 or 4 bucks and replace it, that way there is no doubt.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||06-05-2001||04:10 PM||||The 2.8 has no PVC filter. That's why the throttle body and the inside of the plenum gets so crusty.||||reg||1
Z||000009||84Bill||06-05-2001||06:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>The 2.8 has no PVC filter. That's why the throttle body and the inside of the plenum gets so crusty.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>I did not know this! I'm a 2.5 owner<P>||||reg||11
Z||000010||Seanh||06-05-2001||08:21 PM||||Well, my PCV valve still rattles, and was replaced about 2 months ago so I don't think its bad yet. I will change it again just to be sure though. Anyone know where I can find a new oil cap? I hate to buy from Advance Auto, but I guess if I have to I have to.||||reg||1
